@host = http://localhost:5141
# Paste the "token" from a register/login response:
@token = paste-token-here

### Register (role: CUSTOMER or RIDER)
POST {{host}}/api/Auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ada Customer", "phone": "08012345678", "email": "ada@example.com", "password": "Password123!", "role": "CUSTOMER" }

### Login
POST {{host}}/api/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ada@example.com", "password": "Password123!" }

### Create order (customer). Re-send with the same key: same order comes back, no duplicate.
POST {{host}}/api/Orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Idempotency-Key: order-0001

{ "pickupLat": 6.5244, "pickupLng": 3.3792, "pickupAddress": "Yaba", "dropoffLat": 6.6018, "dropoffLng": 3.3515, "dropoffAddress": "Ikeja Mall" }

### List orders (customers: own; riders: open jobs; admins: all)
GET {{host}}/api/Orders?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Accept order (rider). A second rider accepting the same order gets 409 ORDER_NOT_AVAILABLE.
POST {{host}}/api/Orders/1/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Complete order with the customer's 6-digit code (assigned rider only)
POST {{host}}/api/Orders/1/complete
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "otp": "123456" }

### Rider location ping (5 per 10s per rider, then 429)
POST {{host}}/api/Riders/update-location?lat=6.55&lng=3.36
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Withdraw from your own wallet
POST {{host}}/api/Wallets/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Idempotency-Key: withdraw-0001

{ "amount": 5000, "accountNumber": "0123456789", "bankCode": "058" }

### Admin stats (ADMIN role)
GET {{host}}/api/Admin/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Health
GET {{host}}/health/ready
